The drow are dark elves: a sub-race of elven blood twisted by long ages
beneath the surface in the lightless caverns of the underdark.  Where
their surface cousins claim kinship with the lost Faerie race, the drow
trace their heritage to ancient exiles whose pacts with darker powers
left them gifted with arcane mastery and cursed with the hatred of nearly
every other race.  Surface dwellers regard the drow as something to be
killed on sight; the drow themselves return the sentiment with interest.

Drow males range from 52 to 58 inches and 93 to 120 pounds.
Drow females range from 51 to 57 inches and 73 to 100 lbs.  Their build
is identical to that of surface elves, so equipment crafted for one
fits the other - one of the few practical kinships still binding them.

Drow are gifted spellcasters and thieves, with high intelligence, focus,
and dexterity.  Their charisma is the highest of any playable race - a
gift that serves them well when they must charm or manipulate the few
who will deal with them at all.  They are also among the luckier races,
as if shaped by some patron deity's favor.  These gifts are paid for in
physical frailty: low brawn and constitution leave them poorly suited to
the front line, and a weak constitution combined with a paltry wisdom
means they recover their hit points slowly and learn their skills slower
still.  They are notably less perceptive than other races - long ages
beneath the world have dulled the senses that surface dwellers rely on.

The drow's underdark heritage gives them several gifts.  They have
infravision, allowing them to see in pitch-black rooms where most other
races would be helpless.  Their natural ability to fade into shadow
makes them harder to spot indoors than any other race.  They resist
charm and paralysis, and like their surface cousins they are immune to
magical sleep.

Two innate abilities are theirs by right of blood, accessible through
the 'innate' command.  Drow can wrap themselves briefly in shadow
(invisibility) about twice per game day - long enough to slip past a
patrol or reach a trainer in hostile territory.  Drow can also summon
an unnatural darkness that smothers an entire room for several minutes,
blinding any creature without infravision or true sight - including
themselves.  Both abilities require a few mud hours to recharge between
uses.  See 'help innate' for the command itself, and 'help drow invis'
and 'help drow darkness' for the abilities.

Drow are an advanced race: at least one level-50 character must exist on
the account before drow can be selected during character creation.

A drow's life is hard.  The cityguards of Grimhaven and Brightmoon
attack drow on sight regardless of conduct - the racial outcast status
follows the player into every lawful settlement.  Drow players will
need to rely on stealth and invisibility to reach trainers and shops
in those cities, and even their own race's stronghold in T'ir Na Z'goth
is no sanctuary - the drow within will treat a returning surface-walker
no better than any other intruder.  Disguise and polymorph effects do
hide a drow's true race from cityguards while the disguise holds.

Players choosing drow should be prepared for a more demanding game than
any other playable race offers.

